# records/.gitignore
# Keep the measured-record tree versioned, but exclude the largest
# regenerable artifacts so the checkout stays sane.  The human-readable
# evidence stays tracked; the machine dumps stay on disk but are ignored.
#
# Tracked artifacts are listed explicitly in the curated subdirs' READMEs
# and in the baseline files; this ignore keeps the repo checkout sane.

# ---- qwen35 probe: fp32 tensor dumps + manifest.json per layer ----
# These are regenerable probe outputs, not canonical source.
records/qwen35-probe-2026-10-08/*/manifest.json
records/qwen35-probe-2026-10-08/*/*.f32

# ---- c21 baseline: keep the readable profile.txt + run.log, drop raw CSV/JSON ----
# The profile.txt is the human evidence; CSV/JSON are machine dumps.
records/c21-baseline-2026-10-08/*/profile.csv
records/c21-baseline-2026-10-08/*/profile.json

# ---- llama.cpp reference transcript: keep the curated one, drop the giant raw ----
records/2026-10-07_llamacpp_reference.txt
